<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Azul (Rubén Darío)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1888</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Azul is a collection of short stories and poems by the Nicaraguan poet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ruben-dario">Rubén Darío</a>, published in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valparaiso">Valparaíso</a>, Chile, in 1888. Its refined language, rich imagery and musical verse, drawing on French Parnassian and Symbolist models, made it the founding work of modernismo, the movement that renewed Spanish-language literature. A second, enlarged edition appeared in 1890.</p></div>
